\textbf{Use Case Name} & OEM/OUI Verification \\
\textbf{Description} & Verifies the manufacturer of detected devices
using the Organizationally

Unique Identifier (OUI) portion of the MAC address. \\
\textbf{Primary Actor} & System (automated verification process) \\
\textbf{Secondary Actor} & Administrator (reviews flagged devices) \\
\textbf{Preconditions} & The system has access to OEM API. \\
\textbf{Postconditions} & The system identifies the manufacturer of each
device and flags unrecog-

nized manufacturers. \\
\textbf{Main Flow} & \begin{minipage}[t]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{enumerate}
\def\labelenumi{\arabic{enumi}.}
\item
  \begin{quote}
  The system extracts the OUI from the MAC address.
  \end{quote}
\item
  \begin{quote}
  It matches the OUI against a trusted list of manufacturers.
  \end{quote}
\item
  \begin{quote}
  Devices with unrecognized manufacturers are flagged as suspicious.
  \end{quote}
\end{enumerate}
\end{minipage} \\
\textbf{Alternative Flow} & The system logs devices with incomplete OUI
information for further

review. \\
\textbf{Exceptions} & OUI verification fails if the database of trusted
manufacturers is inaccessi-

ble. \\
\textbf{Result} & The system identifies and validates device
manufacturers. \\
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

