  \protect\hypertarget{_bookmark139}{}{}\textbf{Introduction}
\end{enumerate}

\begin{quote}
Testing and evaluation are crucial stages in the development of the
Rogue Device Detection System. They ensure that the system meets the
requirements defined in the specification phase and operates as intended
under different conditions. This chapter covers various testing methods
used to validate system functionality, accuracy, reliability, and
performance. Additionally, GNS3 was utilized to simulate realistic
network environments for extensive system testing.
\end{quote}

\begin{enumerate}
\def\labelenumi{\arabic{enumi}.}
\setcounter{enumi}{1}
